## Habitability & Strategic Notes

* **Native life:** Perfectly adapted to pressure-uplifted terrain and abyssal gradients
* **Off-world access:**

  * Continental plateaus are the *least lethal* entry points
  * Still require active gravity nullification and structural overengineering
* **Strategic value:**

  * Raised continents act as natural fortress platforms
  * Abyssal oceans serve as planetary armor and resource vaults
  * Conventional surface invasion is functionally impossible

